                <pb facs="0750" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg670"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Powell reports that the Provisional Government will, on October 7, issue
                    decree fixing date on which blockade is to become effective; that the Government
                    states it will, commencing October 10, place armed vessels at Gonaives and St.
                    Marc.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
